    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a high-floor offensive profile, anchored by **Gunnar Henderson**, who leads the squad with an elite 83.29 score against Warren. His projection is bolstered significantly by a massive 16% park factor bump and a 14% platoon edge, making him our primary engine for R and HR. We are also leaning heavily into the matchup against Bassitt, where **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.56) and **Heliot Ramos** (70.57) are poised for big production; the favorable park and SP skill ratings for these two make them mandatory starts over mid-tier options. **Jackson Merrill** (75.10) also demands attention, as his score is inflated by a wind-out scenario and an advantageous platoon matchup, effectively offsetting the minor negative impact of the opponent\u2019s elite catching frame.\n\nWe faced a tight squeeze on the bubble, with **Dominic Smith** (51.11) serving as the most difficult omission. While his park and platoon metrics were positive, the sheer efficiency of **Drake Baldwin** and **Coby Mayo** in their respective spots pushed **Dominic Smith** to the bench to preserve our game caps. Meanwhile, we continue to manage the absence of **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, who remains on the IL, and **Luis Robert Jr.**, who is out of the lineup due to unfavorable platoon splits and rest. Our roster remains well-positioned, though we are monitoring the wind and the specific pitch-framing capabilities of today\u2019s catchers against our speed-focused threats like **Nasim Nunez** and **Sam Antonacci**. We need to ensure that **Nasim Nunez**, despite a sub-optimal ninth-order slot, continues to prioritize contact and stolen base opportunities to maintain his utility value as we push through this mid-August stretch.",
